{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/2026-07-23-what-is-cricket/audio/main-ad7335866507.mp3","durationSec":147.768,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":1.54,"text":"Cricket is played by two teams."},{"start":1.86,"end":3.14,"text":"Each team has eleven players."},{"start":3.7,"end":4.28,"text":"One team bats."},{"start":4.72,"end":6.28,"text":"The other team fields and bowls."},{"start":6.98,"end":9.42,"text":"The batting team tries to score as many runs as possible."},{"start":10.02,"end":12.18,"text":"The fielding team tries to get the batters out."},{"start":12.18,"end":16.42,"text":"An innings can end when ten batters are out or when the team finishes its overs."},{"start":17.06,"end":18.46,"text":"Then the other team bats."},{"start":19.02,"end":21,"text":"The team with more runs usually wins."},{"start":21.86,"end":24.54,"text":"The pitch is a flat strip of ground in the middle of the field."},{"start":25.02,"end":26.34,"text":"It is 22 yards long."},{"start":27.14,"end":28.8,"text":"At each end of the pitch there is a wicket."},{"start":28.8,"end":32.52,"text":"A wicket is made of three wooden sticks called stumps."},{"start":33.08,"end":37.38,"text":"Two small pieces of wood called bails sit on top of the stumps."},{"start":38.14,"end":42,"text":"The bowler stands at one end and sends the ball toward the wicket at the other end."},{"start":42.58,"end":45.42,"text":"The batter stands in front of their wicket to protect it."},{"start":45.98,"end":49.1,"text":"The batter uses a flat bat to hit the ball."},{"start":49.48,"end":53.4,"text":"When the ball is hit, the two batters at the wickets can run to each other’s end."},{"start":54.56,"end":57.14,"text":"Each completed run adds one run to the score."},{"start":58.02,"end":64.08,"text":"If the ball reaches the boundary rope around the field, the batting team gets four runs without running."},{"start":65.38,"end":69.76,"text":"If the ball flies over the boundary without bouncing, the team gets six runs."},{"start":71,"end":73.98,"text":"The bowler runs up and bowls the ball toward the batter."},{"start":75.06,"end":78.26,"text":"The ball may bounce once on the pitch before it reaches the batter."},{"start":79.52,"end":82.22,"text":"Six valid balls from one bowler make one over."},{"start":83.12,"end":86.54,"text":"After each over, a different bowler takes the ball from the other end."},{"start":87.18,"end":89.88,"text":"One bowler cannot bowl two overs in a row."},{"start":89.88,"end":93.16,"text":"There are several ways a batter can be dismissed."},{"start":93.16,"end":97.64,"text":"Bowled means the ball hits the stumps and the bails fall off."},{"start":98.7,"end":103.06,"text":"Caught means a fielder catches a ball hit by the bat before it touches the ground."},{"start":103.06,"end":109.5,"text":"Run out means the batter is outside the crease line when a fielder breaks the wicket with the ball during a run."},{"start":109.5,"end":112.9,"text":"Ten dismissals can end an innings."},{"start":114.02,"end":115.3,"text":"Cricket has three main formats."},{"start":115.3,"end":117.3,"text":"A Test match is the longest."},{"start":117.92,"end":122.1,"text":"Each team can bat in two innings, and the match can last up to five days."},{"start":122.62,"end":127.54,"text":"A One Day International, called an ODI, gives each team 50 overs to bat."},{"start":127.9,"end":129.72,"text":"An ODI usually finishes in one day."},{"start":130.36,"end":135.64,"text":"A Twenty20, called a T20, gives each team only 20 overs."},{"start":136.48,"end":139.1,"text":"A T20 match takes about three hours."},{"start":139.82,"end":142.5,"text":"The ICC Cricket World Cup uses ODI matches."},{"start":142.5,"end":147.16,"text":"The ICC Men’s T20 World Cup uses T20 matches."}],"words":[{"text":"Cricket","start":0,"end":0.26},{"text":"is","start":0.26,"end":0.48},{"text":"played","start":0.48,"end":0.68},{"text":"by","start":0.68,"end":0.9},{"text":"two","start":0.9,"end":1.16},{"t